<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION SLIDES LOWER.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION SLIDES LOWER.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse fell to 5.218 billion litas last week from 5.279 billion</p>
<p>litas the previous week, the stock exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					    June 02-06     May 26-30</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		  15,235	   17,137</p>
<p>    Executed orders		   1,053	    1,157</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)	     911		1,003</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL     2,476,680	3,271,720</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		 71		 77</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	   2,088,100	16,770,300</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week     60,154,585     60,963,522</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week     3,312,849	9,336,514</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	   2,437,150	2,339,880</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	   2,088,100	16,770,300</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	   6		  10</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	 39,530	   931,840</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
